# Dear ImGui (M5: the editor shell) — TWO pins, on purpose.
#
# libs/imgui.tag    the upstream snapshot that gets FETCHED. A tag is the only
#                   thing that survives a mirror, a tarball proxy or a
#                   corporate git cache without server-side SHA-in-want.
# libs/imgui.commit the commit that tag must resolve to, and the bootstrap
#                   VERIFIES it. The tag is therefore never authoritative: if
#                   upstream re-points or re-tags it, the bootstrap fails
#                   loudly instead of silently rebuilding the editor against
#                   different ImGui code.
#
# The Docking branch, not master: ROADMAP M5 asks for a docking shell, and
# migrating an imgui.ini layout between the two branches is a user-visible
# migration nobody wants to ship twice.

b48d1afbe8ee8b238e2961dc363a949dd7304e23
